    "error_map": {
        "400": "invalid_request",
        "401": "auth_expired",
        "403": "permission_denied",
        "404": "invalid_request",
        "500": "provider_transient",
        "502": "provider_transient",
        "503": "provider_transient",
        "504": "provider_transient"
    },
    "_error_map_note": "Story 28.2 decision (dossier section 6): TTD publishes no numeric error-code table, so the map keys are HTTP-STATUS-ONLY and the CONNECTOR applies them itself (module-side status lookup with classify_http_error as fallback). Body-token refinements: a 401/403 body containing 'revoked' or 'disabled' -> auth_revoked (reconnect) instead of auth_expired/permission_denied. A 401 during a report call re-authenticates once (ExpirationDateUtc passed) before classifying. A Failed ReportExecutionState maps to the canonical 'expired' poll status when the failureReason is not configuration (single socle resubmission, then provider_transient); configuration failureReasons (invalid/not supported/unknown dimension|metric/template) raise invalid_request. 429 stays on the core.quota.RateLimitError breaker path (Retry-After UNDOCUMENTED -> default backoff), never in this map.",
    "refetch": {
        "nightly_days": 3,
        "weekly_days": 14,
        "monthly_days": 45,
        "_note": "Dossier section 5: conversion families (click/view-through/touch/time-weighted-decay, pixels 01-06) restate as attribution windows close; treat the last ~3-7 days as provisional (nightly 3). The exact attribution window is ReportTemplate-configured (probe-only). Weekly 14 / monthly 45 cover the restatement tail. AD-7 supersede-by-pull_id makes every re-pull idempotent."
    },
